   "type": "access-law",
   "text": "Wyoming stream access (WGFD): \"the land underneath most of Wyoming's streams and lakes is owned by the adjacent property owner\" — next to private land, boaters \"must have permission from the landowner to wade, drop their anchor or get out of their boats. Wyoming law allows boaters to float across private lands and portage around features such as logjams, fences and diversion structures.\" Launch and take out only at public sites.",
